  "reason": "The evidence strongly establishes that multiprofile + scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted + imagenet_vit_l (config_025, acc=0.725) is the current best, and that RNA encoder choice is critical (scgpt drops accuracy to 0.52). The one major untested dimension is PCA (pca_n2000) as RNA encoder, which is fundamentally different from both scvi (learned nonlinear) and scgpt (learned generative). Config_019 pairs PCA with the best-known settings (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile) to directly test whether a linear RNA representation can be competitive. If PCA performs near scvi_n200, it opens a new direction; if it underperforms significantly (like scgpt), it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and the remaining 3 experiments can focus on fine-tuning around the current best. With 3 experiments left, resolving this key uncertainty is the highest-value use of the next slot."
}

